WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.594 --> 00:00:17.657
the prizes were given out, it was time to eat them.

2
00:00:19.538 --> 00:00:24.763
Alice did not eat her thimble, of course, but the other creatures ate their candy.

3
00:00:26.204 --> 00:00:30.788
The large birds complained that the candy was so small, they couldn't taste it.

4
00:00:32.716 --> 00:00:37.299
The small birds coughed and choked on their candy because it was so large.

5
00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.322
But after a while everyone settled down.

6
00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:49.086
The creatures sat in a circle and begged the Mouse to tell them his story.

7
00:00:49.106 --> 00:00:53.648
"You promised to tell me about your family," Alice said.

8
00:00:53.668 --> 00:00:56.770
"And why you hate C and D."

9
00:00:57.731 --> 00:00:59.852
She didn't say "cats and dogs."

10
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.621
She didn't want to upset the Mouse again.

11
00:01:02.641 --> 00:01:08.545
"Mine is a long and sad tale," the Mouse began.

12
00:01:10.066 --> 00:01:11.808
Alice studied the mouse's body.

13
00:01:11.828 --> 00:01:17.371
"You definitely have a long tail, but I don't understand why it's sad."

14
00:01:18.752 --> 00:01:22.335
"No, not my tail," the Mouse said impatiently.

15
00:01:22.355 --> 00:01:25.577
"My tale, as in story."

16
00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:30.040
He went on talking.

17
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.442
Meanwhile Alice kept thinking about words that sound alike but have different meanings.

18
00:01:38.462 --> 00:01:43.525
"Now do you understand why I don't like cats?"

19
00:01:44.065 --> 00:01:45.265
the Mouse said to Alice.

20
00:01:45.285 --> 00:01:48.547
"What?" Alice looked at him and blinked.

21
00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.768
"You weren't paying attention!"

22
00:01:52.128 --> 00:01:53.489
the Mouse said angrily.

23
00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:57.491
"I don't know why I bothered telling you this story."

24
00:01:58.451 --> 00:01:59.792
He started to walk away.

25
00:02:01.028 --> 00:02:03.490
Alice felt bad that she had upset him again.

26
00:02:07.734 --> 00:02:09.155
come back and repeat your story!"

27
00:02:09.515 --> 00:02:10.536
she called after him.

28
00:02:10.556 --> 00:02:14.079
"I promise to listen to every word this time."

29
00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:19.503
"Yes, please do come back," all the others said together.

30
00:02:20.885 --> 00:02:24.948
But the Mouse only shook his head impatiently and walked faster.

31
00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:29.492
"What a pity he wouldn't stay."

32
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.420
The Parrot sighed.

33
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.061
"I wish Dinah was here," Alice said.

34
00:02:35.081 --> 00:02:37.142
"She would fetch him for us."

35
00:02:37.162 --> 00:02:42.063
"And who is Dinah, if I may ask?"

36
00:02:42.463 --> 00:02:43.284
the Parrot said.

37
00:02:43.304 --> 00:02:44.984
"Dinah's my cat.

38
00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:47.125
She's so good at catching mice."

39
00:02:48.265 --> 00:02:52.966
Alice replied eagerly, for she was always happy to talk about her pet.

40
00:02:52.987 --> 00:02:56.247
"And you should see her chasing birds!"

41
00:02:58.948 --> 00:03:04.170
All the birds started talking at once, and some hurried away as fast as they could.

42
00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:10.733
One old magpie began wrapping himself in a scarf.

43
00:03:10.753 --> 00:03:12.394
"I really must be going.

44
00:03:13.414 --> 00:03:16.075
This air is bad for my throat!"

45
00:03:19.197 --> 00:03:24.319
A canary called out in a trembling voice to her children, "Come away, my dears.

46
00:03:24.779 --> 00:03:26.360
It's time for us to go home."

47
00:03:33.424 --> 00:03:35.385
Alice was soon left all alone.

48
00:03:35.406 --> 00:03:40.609
"I wish I'd never mentioned Dinah," she said sadly.

49
00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:46.333
"Nobody seems to like her down here, but I think she's the best cat in the world.

50
00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:48.614
Oh, Dinah!

51
00:03:50.576 --> 00:03:52.357
I wonder if I'll ever see you again!"

52
00:03:53.418 --> 00:03:57.901
Poor Alice began to cry because she felt so lonely and sad.

53
00:03:59.522 --> 00:04:02.404
In a little while, however, she heard footsteps.

54
00:04:03.228 --> 00:04:07.572
She looked up eagerly, hoping that the Mouse had changed his mind and was coming back.

55
00:04:08.793 --> 00:04:11.255
But once again it was the White Rabbit.

56
00:04:12.336 --> 00:04:17.721
This time he was walking slowly and looking anxiously about, as if he'd lost something.

57
00:04:19.943 --> 00:04:22.005
Alice heard him muttering to himself.

58
00:04:22.025 --> 00:04:24.106
"The Duchess!

59
00:04:24.447 --> 00:04:25.448
The Duchess!"

60
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.212
the White Rabbit said as he looked high and low.

61
00:04:33.616 --> 00:04:34.716
"Oh, my paws!

62
00:04:35.177 --> 00:04:37.037
Oh, my fur and whiskers!

63
00:04:37.857 --> 00:04:41.278
The Duchess is going to be so angry if I'm late!

64
00:04:42.238 --> 00:04:44.219
I wonder where I could have dropped them.

65
00:04:45.059 --> 00:04:46.740
I don't see them anywhere!"

66
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.841
Alice guessed right away that he was looking for his gloves and fan.

67
00:04:54.422 --> 00:04:58.243
She happily began hunting for them, but they were nowhere to be seen.

68
00:04:59.643 --> 00:05:02.024
In fact, everything had changed.

69
00:05:03.184 --> 00:05:05.346
She seemed to be outdoors now.

70
00:05:06.487 --> 00:05:10.892
The great hall with the glass table and little door had disappeared.
